{#
_grid.html.twig — the calendar itself, and the one place that picks a view's
layout.

Rendered by the docked pane and by the full page. Month and agenda are the same
markup in both. Day and week are not, and that is the only difference between
the two shapes of this app:

  the page  a time-grid — hours down the side, every event drawn where it
            actually is and as long as it actually is, and draggable.
  the pane  the column list, unchanged. Seven columns of positioned blocks
            behind a time gutter need roughly a screen's width to be legible;
            the pane is ~380px of a row it shares with the mail, so a grid there
            would be seven slivers and an unreadable axis.

**The choice is made on `isPane`, which the controller passes in, and never on
a media query.** The pane is narrow on a 2560px monitor as well as on a laptop,
so the window's width does not answer the question — and CSS that rendered both
and hid one would ship a drag-and-drop controller to a pane that cannot use it,
and double the markup of every calendar render to throw half of it away.
CalendarView::isTimeGrid() answers the other half: which views have a time axis
worth drawing at all.

This replaces an earlier note on _view_days.html.twig promising that a time-grid
"belongs with drag-to-move, which is its own piece of work". That work is done;
what survives of the promise is the pane's column list, which the reasoning was
always really about.

The scroll container differs between the two branches on purpose. The column
list scrolls as one block, so the wrapper owns the overflow. The time-grid keeps
its day headers and its all-day band pinned while only the hours scroll, so it
owns its own scrolling and this wrapper must not add a second scrollbar around
it.
#}

{% set days = range.days %}
{% set isPane = isPane|default(false) %}
{% set isTimeGrid = view.isTimeGrid and not isPane %}

{% if isTimeGrid %}
    <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col" data-controller="calendar--grid">
        {% include 'calendar/_view_timegrid.html.twig' %}
    </div>
{% else %}
    <div class="flex-1 min-h-0 overflow-y-auto" data-controller="calendar--grid">
        {% if view.value == 'month' %}
            {% include 'calendar/_view_month.html.twig' %}
        {% elseif view.value == 'agenda' %}
            {% include 'calendar/_view_agenda.html.twig' %}
        {% else %}
            {% include 'calendar/_view_days.html.twig' %}
        {% endif %}
    </div>
{% endif %}
